==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|sleier}}, {{m|gmh|sleiger}}, {{m|gmh|sloiger}}, {{m|gmh|slogier}}. Of {{unc|de|nocap=1}} ultimate origin, but most likely borrowed; perhaps related to {{der|de|la|stragulus|t=covering}}.

Compare {{cog|gml|sleyer}}, {{m|gml|sloier}}, {{m|gml|sloiger}}, {{cog|enm|scleire}}, {{m|enm|scleyre}}, {{m|enm|sleyre}}, {{m|enm|slyre|t=veil}}.

